# Commit Message Convention

- Use Conventional Commits with an English type and optional scope.
- Write the commit description in Chinese, matching the style of existing history.
- Make the description specific and reasonably detailed: include the affected area,
  user-visible behavior, and the key purpose of the change when they fit.
- For changes spanning multiple behaviors, add a commit body describing the main
  implementation details and verification instead of compressing everything into
  a vague one-line summary.

Example: `fix(content): 同步成人模式并修复移动端确认弹窗层级`
